  "workflow_name": "Monte Carlo Charge Transport Simulation",
  "definition": "This workflow family encompasses Monte Carlo simulations of charge carrier transport in semiconductor materials and nanostructures, where carriers are treated semiclassically with scattering from phonons, impurities, and interfaces. The workflow involves defining the electronic band structure (valleys, subbands), computing scattering rates from Fermi's golden rule, simulating carrier trajectories under an electric field using Monte Carlo methods, and extracting steady-state transport properties such as distribution functions, drift velocity, mobility, and subband populations.",
